question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=4f(x)+7,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4f(x).$\n\n![](images/17/178f32ee899fe88c09207e080727689f151fa17b1fb5591f2d689e90dcf4e46e.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $7$ units to get the graph of $y=4f(x)+7.$\n\n![](images/5c/5c1e620fbb2d3de5bb27519464b931aa9d7bce9043e2f9e1a33d52897849e31d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4aee0a3-1694-5a48-a21d-afd11f01889f" :knowledge-point/title "Graph Transformations Containing Vertical Translations and Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73084097-73cc-5282-8abf-a8a5a5f97b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/63/6302fd971dd1a48d9931506613163a007ec295b5d2ccd7ce6235a2dbeee6874f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525497} {:answer/id #uuid "8d19e195-4664-55cd-a091-80295118d88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b2e03334bdb74506d9ed542656943f99ca86142686d1b5368eae4e05527d4e35.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525558} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3981ba-80e1-58f4-a8bc-29fd059f3013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d1680c140c0c1b32ffb5ee17e7ab379e55de6844668a439561080e4b1bc631e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525640} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e08692-cdad-5be9-a29c-6c873bf