s, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(3x),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(3x).$\n\n![](images/f6/f6743a24307e16fbe5df98bf2ec3a34c5aa5673e2255cdfbd2aa65c9cc9e6aee.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(3x).$\n\n![](images/a8/a88eb4b9d68be3b491a00fc3ed9a738a6a2703f3658bbc131e8348c9498a0bfa.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2456098c-d6ed-5d85-a1a1-69ad54f02216" :knowledge-point/title "Other Cases of Graphing Transformations Containing Two Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e86425-4835-53d9-998b-58b1a80b257c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/88/8889881f0dc07f308492edd561f784d631ca08cdae29e7eb765624ed0485563f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525476} {:answer/id #uuid "93379f1f-6871-5619-a565-4c3b028d0ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d125f9a013424b3019fc5935a822bf9c4a282c59f786e933349c59cf89004d0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525579} {:answer/id #uuid "ad278f2c-baae-5709-ad2a-74e0766e5631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb0db551bdd8108078ae9d14897c534de6ffbaab664873736240e29992ad0751.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525644} {:answer/id #uuid "b05d28b1-1ef8-52db-b108-33b592563250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5da93f533eede4494b75f31d81e3dd2b5bb0916d5f4d16894adf5d4a2c6cd8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525652} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6e9a4d-52f9-5b56-9b6e-b400fa2db9fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fb9badb4fb9f6fbfcada362cb217f64faacce5c1e9c19b81f325c78e1fc8f65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe6e9a4d-52f9-5b56-9b6e-b400fa2db9fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fb9badb4fb9f6fbfcada362cb217f64faacce5c1e9c19b81f325c78e1fc8f65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525838} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc83b95f-a922-5dbb-8c6a-b520b1e028d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9424b3c1-d470-5046-9c40-b1dfb0dc13d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-112935" :question/problem "![](images/70/70c4581f3b802172e5d66a514eda3a37293f7ab2bf65ef6dcccb8073832e5f96.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=2f(x-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=2f(x-3),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it right by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=f(x-3).$\n\n![](images/c9/c9ac259b9e9a907a8c00053bdb1818f44226f126b3544358dc98c1329a5617af.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=2f(x-3).$\n\n![](images/75/757800fd367f695175be1cb991b62ae0a576eec9ee1e0018a08d56c945ec6de7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4aee0a3-1694-5a48-a21d-afd11f01889f" :knowledge-point/title "Graph Transformations Containing Vertical Translations and Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bbb887-0e61-5e4f-bbf9-cec0976def71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/727240355e0330dc9a84c245276535eab5e867e257de891ccc72b72bacad38c7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525224} {:answer/id #uuid "22d81245-8cbc-5c11-ac56-8c07161b202e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/856fc3559d3835ce2c639e980a52221743a69683e1c2327bbe4160424b871435.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525286} {:answer/id #uuid "48426ed9-9b40-5e23-9e5f-5decf6655974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/15a356832582f12619c2394f50d0402ce10198d80e73c8ff239d1162f7e2657c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525386} {:answer/id #uuid "637f718a-6432-5106-a4a2-3d14229b1da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6d/6d0ed51b93fa731e94184ac5fb07a8efa091ee918d4fa01d2f5142ce068d73dc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525458} {:answer/id #uuid "9e765cd3-6894-5955-b005-bc9417431fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc15f288be183505fd495a1c2fe08efa99baf0ad502e8ca3fd7d9e0faecc677e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d81245-8cbc-5c11-ac56-8c07161b202e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/856fc3559d3835ce2c639e980a52221743a69683e1c2327bbe4160424b871435.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525286} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3dd18a-fc6f-5632-80b2-9226272898a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62a6fa3a-202f-5d9e-a258-2bf57d4dce4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-87102" :question/problem "![](images/ed/edb2f75e0e5ba2d16afde5e335b8adc888a621d7e24720fab45a397bc6fb497d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=4f(x)+2?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=4f(x)+2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4f(x).$\n\n![](images/23/231d9ba40de9b7a061dd56be38b4145f3fd11b8488535957b8317c7c0e3c1cef.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=4f(x)+2.$\n\n![](images/95/95fce5c1cbcf16e036d4fe86a526c1910acd2b49dec8ac31e1641b137ef929df.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100947 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb2265f-df80-53ac-bcab-90c7925a4e86" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Transformations Containing Horizontal and Vertical Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b5c415-60c9-50af-aab7-a1a9461c2a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/8313361502dee5a7e8db9ad4c49f58519d40638f1c368c7f7263ec42ae3cc4ce.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525419} {:answer/id #uuid "7669637a-c893-53a2-af5d-b0f78a28ac68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/301b659957b99a24a35609