 followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(2x),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(2x).$\n\n![](images/73/736295268bc4b0832b7288c71f5e6721748d86a586127be5b423d3f71a7726f1.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(2x).$\n\n![](images/b7/b7519d9dec6ab7f0d465e68a1a72068db28d7639aa4b4710ce86a1eb0083d24a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100947 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb2265f-df80-53ac-bcab-90c7925a4e86" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Transformations Containing Horizontal and Vertical Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b77fb03-0e8f-5bdb-a62a-cd454390d957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/af606e33e00156f567f5fea87a0c6d5730775fd9f05bfda5f0498d294384f2d1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525395} {:answer/id #uuid "5a94c15a-4b22-523c-9d8b-faa505cf7c3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e84cdb5e51258a1aba0022f46dc031e5aeff6ef06c186cee8efcac28d5177bc4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525438} {:answer/id #uuid "78e22db9-65e0-53cb-bb23-cbfbac8e5374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/82881c772ec725bee0e8aaa6f34b698fa2be53236118b690aeb95a4ae987997b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525508} {:answer/id #uuid "b8623f0e-89e5-5b96-aa54-9cb4bcd7a2f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a7557a85cb5f7ffaedc4bc921dee30f0d7e6535a351ba604158644f957e476