to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4f(\\frac{1}{3}x).$\n\n![](images/28/28fc05b5ed03768282704609a1d4c05e5c579e75bca0bd5c9f4776c460fe8ae1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100947 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fb2265f-df80-53ac-bcab-90c7925a4e86" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Transformations Containing Horizontal and Vertical Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0055e42f-0988-571a-a4f6-08aad9a4c758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/afa4e893afa12e6b99cf1782285b65e6d471a410dbb884e3cc847ea68c21651b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525208} {:answer/id #uuid "10690c8e-b46f-557d-af22-f50b3991ef63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3f/3fa2f1e3c02cedb55037828ac9b04c9ad5e67ca24b6f3fee0c9c37da69bff377.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525242} {:answer/id #uuid "56d1a1b5-0641-5646-905c-823c512e6e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/43/432e12fa9f32b162ebbfed564d76513d119cc8e886bf9800005f360cfaf900f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525430} {:answer/id #uuid "9c98feb0-9d74-566c-97db-e58c218d9fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0ab6fc6723862a48cf5304bbe1c1ad42a9ff3cfe9ab941b165475cd065b51f1a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525604} {:answer/id #uuid "c32be768-3700-5814-991e-eab6ec68a41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8aab71e494539cafa93f1769e62a162b4a2a98e755dc65a834deafaf6a91332f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c98feb0-9d74-566c-97db-e58c218d9fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0ab6fc6723862a48cf5304bbe1c1ad42a9ff3cfe9ab941b165475cd065b51f1a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525604} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed4a604-6986-5caa-a64a-604acfb10d3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1dc940f3-d894-5aef-acf1-d5fe41dbd6a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-87147" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3c459cda9cd4cf2c1cb6b0a84b66108fab84d59a87bd14ed11b6ea80cbf8212.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=2f(4x)?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=2f(4x),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(4x).$\n\n![](images/2f/2fe8a51d1b19bbe18f90b80692df31a01debd536a46569104b1e01a18f2bae87.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=2f(4x).$\n\n![](images/d3/d3865abcbb54d17f0af7594c7c50de9301e795b7ac1c364b180e782aa0cf94be.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100946 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23014f0a-c381-5997-9f41-2734d3102280" :knowledge-point/title "Graph Transformations Containing Horizontal Translations and Stretches Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be7eede-e167-5c13-8ad5-b830a9988ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/val